jobs.description:
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Game Designer&lt;/strong&gt; to serve on and elevate the experience on Wheel of Fortune!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the sole Design owner on Wheel of Fortune and reporting directly to the Game Director, this is a unique opportunity to work on a small &amp;amp; mighty Team and put your stamp on a beloved Franchise played across the globe and live for over a decade!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role has it all: helping to define the product roadmap, ensuring that each user experience is flawless, and anything in between. You will be expected to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product, Engineering, Art, Analytics, LiveOps and QA to bring compelling features from concept to release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and update design specs that contain the right level of detail while staying concise and easy to understand for the whole team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help plan our Production roadmap and Liveops calendar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive feature optimizations to maintain gameplay quality, improve balance, and boost player engagement (levels &amp;amp; puzzles, battle pass, weekly and daily challenges, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a Design Owner mentality, ensuring designs meet the player’s needs, the franchise strategy and the business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow the most recent market trends and best practices to create the best possible designs for our roadmap features, and to bring new ideas to the table&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-5 years of professional game design experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency with level design, systems design, game tuning, content design, user experience design and overall design documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of free-to-play monetization mechanics including game balancing and virtual economy management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills - remotely and in person - with the ability to gather feedback, align stakeholders, and iterate to success collaboratively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working independently while thriving in a highly dynamic and international environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with the ability to use data to improve designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working as a Game Designer in free-to-play mobile gaming with a focus on casual/social and/or word/trivia genre&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the Wheel of Fortune TV show, its gameplay and rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that!&amp;nbsp; We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players togeth

&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a superstar &lt;strong&gt;Game Design Director&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Star Trek Fleet Command team in the UK, working remotely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day – whether in our work environments alongside talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing, and innovating in the mobile games industry, connecting millions of players around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Star Trek Fleet Command&lt;/strong&gt; is a standout success in the gaming industry. Launched in 2018, our in-house developed 4X MMO has continually evolved, earning its place as one of the top-grossing games on the market. Our next chapter is bold: we’re evolving the traditional 4X experience in STFC — and we need a bold design leader to shape the content and loops our players engage with on a daily basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Game Design Director on STFC, you’ll own the standards, direction, and experiences that define how millions of players experience growth and mastery across our monthly content releases and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become the design owner and leader behind our content pipeline, directing designers and live ops specialists in crafting compelling experiences for our players&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide teams through the creative process, ensuring they can hit the vision of the game and deliver upon player and product needs with accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor designers in systems and economy design to elevate our standards and craft incredible experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fostering a high-performance culture within the department through leadership, people development, and team engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the design process to ensure the standards of players are met and exceeded&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with design leaders to shape the future of the game economy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Experienced, driven and passionate Designers, Product Managers, Analysts, and Engineers to implement features which aim to advance the genre&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate performance using data, player feedback, and your own playtest experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for scale: plan for long-term content extensibility and system health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of game design leadership experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in F2P systems design and progression modelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience designing systems or economies for live, F2P games (preferably MMO, 4X, or strategy genres)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience and mastery of complex game economies in F2P&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership and team management skills, with the ability to inspire and motivate a design team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of delivering clear, consistent creative direction and managerial feedback that elevates others&#39; work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with all aspects of game design discipline: concept, game progression, interface, monetization, and retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate KPI targets and data into design direction for teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of spreadsheets and confidence in balancing power curves, pacing, and resource flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally and navigating live production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive, thoughtful, and collaborative approach to game development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the 4X genre with specific experience in F2P 4X&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SQL, scripti

&lt;p&gt;Riot engineers bring deep knowledge of specific technical areas but also value the opportunity to work in a variety of broader domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Unreal Ecosystem (UnEco) team has an impact on a wide array of topics, including runtime performance, tooling, CI/CD, just to name a few. As a Staff Software Engineer on the UnEco team, you&#39;ll drive the technical direction of your team and influence strategy across related teams, building a strong engineering vision and offering creative solutions to technical problems that empower game teams across Riot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team collaborates globally with partners across Riot, all contributing to a stronger, more efficient Unreal development ecosystem. You&#39;ll lead the breakdown of complex, cross-team technical challenges - from build systems to editor tooling to runtime infrastructure - championing solutions in alignment with game teams and partners that empower the developers who depend on your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a full-time role based in Australia (AEST timezone). Internal Job Title: Software Engineer III&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work arrangement: &lt;/strong&gt;Sydney-based Rioters work on-site. Remote work is available for candidates elsewhere in AEST-aligned Australia (e.g. Melbourne, Brisbane, Canberra) with Australian work rights. Perth and Darwin are not suitable due to timezone overlap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocation &amp;amp; Immigration Support: &lt;/strong&gt;Candidates who require visa sponsorship must be based in, or relocate to, Sydney. Riot offers relocation assistance and will sponsor the appropriate work visa, subject to eligibility and local immigration requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, development, and maintenance of shared libraries, plugins, and tools used by multiple game teams - driving platform-wide consistency and maintainability while balancing individual team needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical roadmapping for platform capabilities, setting direction that balances immediate game team needs with long-term architectural vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion technical designs in alignment with game teams and partners, navigating tradeoffs and building consensus across diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and participate in the technical planning process, breaking down multi-month work efforts and sequencing delivery across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold a high standard of engineering excellence. Lead code reviews, drive testing strategy, and contribute to continuous improvement of team and cross-team practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear documentation and communicate technical details across teams and disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and participate in the on-call rotation; resolve live incidents, drive RCAs, and champion systemic fixes to reduce future impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers on the team in both technical and soft skills; help level up developers across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, or a comparable field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years experience in professional software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of professional experience and proficiency with C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software engineering fundamentals (data structures, algorithms, concurrency, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading technical work that impacts multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving technical direction, designing solutions, and reviewing the designs of others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building software used by other engineering teams and navigating cross-team dependencies, rather than deep single-team, single-feature ownership.&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;p&gt;作为一名游戏设计师，你将负责设计、调整并优化玩家体验。你出色的分析能力、对玩家的洞察力以及创造力将共同打造游戏内外令人惊喜且具有吸引力的玩家体验。你将与跨学科团队合作，充分运用各种工具，持续迭代和优化以玩家为核心的设计，致力于让全球数百万玩家感到满意与喜爱。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;在研发（R&amp;amp;D）团队中担任战斗游戏设计师。你将与其他设计师、艺术家和工程师密切协作，优化和迭代以玩家为中心的设计，致力于创造突破性的游戏体验。由于团队规模仍较小，该岗位需要大量实操工作，亲自创建和调校战斗系统/机制。你应能适应目标与限制主要由团队驱动的不确定性环境，同时适应大大小小的变更作为设计流程的日常一部分。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;职责：&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;设计、实现并改进战斗机制与系统，使其令玩家满意并提升对游戏概念的信心。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;在所处游戏类型中探索创新战斗设计方案，提出多种可行的设计与解决方案，清晰说明各种方案之间的权衡与风险。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;利用快速原型与游戏测试验证设计方案的可行性。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;编写清晰的设计文档，确保非设计人员也能评估与实现相关内容。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;与设计团队及其他跨职能团队协作，共同打造出色的整体游戏体验。积极配合、听取反馈并不断迭代，以实现最高质量的产品。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;岗位要求：&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;至少 3 年专业游戏设计工作经验。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;至少 2 年 Unreal 引擎使用经验，熟练使用技能编辑器、关卡编辑器、GAS 系统及蓝图。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;在以下领域至少精通一项：战斗机制、战斗手感、战斗 AI、角色控制 / 摄像机 / 操作系统。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;能够流利使用中文普通话交流。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;加分项：&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;在至少一款已发行游戏中，熟练使用某款游戏引擎的脚本编程。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;能流利使用英语进行口头与书面交流。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;在此岗位中，你将通过精湛的专业技能、积极的协作精神和以玩家愉悦体验为导向的决策获得成功。我们将重点参考你过往的学习经历、工作经验及你与游戏的个人关系。如果你具有强烈的玩家同理心，并真正关心玩家的游戏体验，这份工作可能正是为你量身打造的！&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;用工性质：与专业人事服务公司FESCO Adecco签订劳动合同&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;作为一名系统策划，您将肩负项目城池发展和核心系统玩法的设计工作，围绕成长、建造、资源流、功能解锁等内容，为游戏世界注入持久成长驱动力。您需要以玩家为中心，完善系统框架，设计富有策略深度的城市发展玩法，持续优化成长体验与动力体系，为产品生命周期注入源源不绝的新鲜感。您将与团队高效协作，推动高质量交付并持续提升团队创新能力。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;我们是谁&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;我们以玩家体验为根本，不断追求设计创新。这里是你释放创新想法、赋能核心系统、改变传统玩法生态的大舞台。如果你渴望挑战、热爱运营和创新，期待你加入我们并共创未来！&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;您的影响&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;定义城池发展体验&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;以项目目标为指引，主导城市成长、建筑升级、功能体系等玩法核心模块设计，营造激励成长与多元选择并存的体验节奏。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;构建系统与成长闭环&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;搭建资源生产、消耗、成长及动力体系，让玩家在可感知的反馈循环中体验长期目标与阶段感成就。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;推动系统创新与落地&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;将创意转化为高落地性的系统方案，主导原型验证与功能优化，不断提升成长体系与城池玩法的策略深度。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;跨团队协作推动优质交付&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;联合美术、程序、数值、UI等多团队，保障系统设计与开发同步迭代、品质稳定，并持续聚焦用户体验提升。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;数据驱动与行业洞察&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;关注市场标杆产品及行业趋势，结合数据分析和玩家反馈持续优化系统内容与成长曲线，提升竞争力与可玩性。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;岗位职责&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;参与城池、建筑、资源及系统功能的0到1设计，实现成长、建造、运营等核心模块的系统化梳理与体验优化。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;负责制定成长体系、资源产消与动力闭环相关文档与设计原型，把控系统机制的全周期推演和调优。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;联合数值策划完成系统数值结构、资源分配及发展节奏的详细设定，实现公平性与可玩性平衡。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;跟踪竞品并提炼差异化优势，提出城建及玩法创新点，高效转换为可执行的功能方案，推动快速迭代与落地。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;配合研发、美术等协作团队，确保方案落地还原度和功能流畅，持续推动体验打磨和流程优化。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;收集数据、分析玩家反馈，系统性评估和优化设计内容，推动城池发展和核心系统可持续进化。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;任职要求&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;本科及以上学历，2年以上系统策划或城市成长相关经验，参与过上线产品的核心系统设计与迭代优先。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;熟悉城池建设、养成、系统成长等相关机制，对经济系统、成长体系有系统认知与实操经验。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;拥有扎实的玩法设计、系统梳理、文档输出与流程拆解能力，能独立承担重点模块并协作推进复盘。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;关心用户长期体验，对成长驱动力和多元可玩性有深入洞察，善于结合数据分析优化系统内容。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;具备出色的沟通与团队协作能力，积极推动方案高效落地。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;加分项&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;有城市建设、成长模拟、策略或重社交手游的玩法及系统策划经验。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;具备大型成长/经济系统模型搭建、数据调优或A/B测试实际经验。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;有国际化项目、海外用户洞察或多文化团队协作能力。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;能撰写或阅读英文系统策划文档。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;我们的福利&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;我们倡导健康平衡的工作与生活，提供有竞争力的带薪休假、灵活办公方式及多元保险福利。团队关注多元与包容性氛围，鼓励创新协作，让每一位成员都能获得成长和成就。与我们一起，见证并驱动一款创新大作的诞生吧！&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;用工性质：与专业人事服务公司FESCO Adecco签订劳动合同&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Riot Games was established in 2006 by entrepreneurial gamers who believe that player-focused game development can result in great games. In 2009, Riot released its debut title&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;to critical and player acclaim. As the most played video game in the world, over 100 million play every month. Players form the foundation of our community and it’s for them that we continue to evolve and improve the&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for humble but ambitious, razor-sharp professionals who can teach us a thing or two. We promise to return the favor. Like us, you take play seriously; you’re passionate about games. We embrace those who see things differently, aren’t afraid to experiment, and who have a healthy disregard for constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&#39;s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Game Designer, you will design, tweak, and optimize the player experience. Your analytical skills, player insight, and creativity help craft in- and out-of-game experiences that engage and surprise players. You will collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and work with every tool at hand to create and iterate player-focused designs that will delight millions around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Game Designer (Systems – Balancing &amp;amp; Economy)&lt;/strong&gt; on the &lt;strong&gt;Unpublished R&amp;amp;D Product&lt;/strong&gt; team, you will help design, build, and refine gameplay systems that support engaging player experiences. You will partner with designers, artists, and engineers to develop, iterate, and improve systems through rapid prototyping, testing, and cross-functional collaboration. This role requires a hands-on designer who is comfortable working in an evolving development environment, balancing experimentation with thoughtful decision-making while continuously improving gameplay systems and player experiences. &lt;strong&gt;You will report into the Game Director of the team.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and improve gameplay systems that deliver engaging player experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop multiple system design solutions and clearly communicate implementation trade-offs and associated risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish design principles and best practices for future systems design work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead small cross-functional teams to develop gameplay systems aligned with product objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear design documentation that can be understood and implemented across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with designers, artists, engineers, and production partners to create cohesive player experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize prototyping, playtesting, and data-informed iteration to validate and improve system designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incorporate feedback and continuously refine systems to achieve high-quality player experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of professional experience in Game Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in one or more of the following areas: progression systems, game balance, economy systems, or mathematical modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning gameplay features or leading systems design efforts for at least one shipped title.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to create and improve complex gameplay mechanics and systems with consideration for player experience and long-term maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating multiple gameplay systems into cohesive player experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in Mandarin Chinese.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading systems, economy, or game balance design.&lt;/li

&lt;p&gt;Riot Games was established in 2006 by entrepreneurial gamers who believe that player-focused game development can result in great games. In 2009, Riot released its debut title&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;to critical and player acclaim. As the most played video game in the world, over 100 million play every month. Players form the foundation of our community and it’s for them that we continue to evolve and improve the&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for humble but ambitious, razor-sharp professionals who can teach us a thing or two. We promise to return the favor. Like us, you take play seriously; you’re passionate about games. We embrace those who see things differently, aren’t afraid to experiment, and who have a healthy disregard for constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&#39;s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Game Designer, you will design, tweak, and optimize the player experience. Your analytical skills, player insight, and creativity help craft in- and out-of-game experiences that engage and surprise players. You will collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and work with every tool at hand to create and iterate player-focused designs that will delight millions around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Game Designer (Combat)&lt;/strong&gt; on the Unpublished R&amp;amp;D Product team, you will contribute to early-stage development efforts exploring future player experiences at Riot. You will partner with designers, artists, and engineers to iterate on player-focused designs and help shape engaging gameplay systems. Working within a small and evolving team, you will take a hands-on role in creating and tuning combat systems and mechanics. You will operate in an environment with evolving goals and constraints, where iteration and adaptability are key to success. You will report into the Game Director of the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and improve combat mechanics and systems that satisfy players and increase confidence in the game concept.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek opportunities for innovative combat design solutions within the genre. Create and provide multiple potential designs and solutions. Articulate trade-offs and risks between different options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create high level principles and best practices for future combat design work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize rapid prototyping and playtesting where applicable to validate solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear design documentation that can be evaluated and implemented by non-designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with the design team and other disciplines to create a great holistic experience. Collaborate, receive feedback, and iterate towards the highest quality product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1q9kxa&quot; data-start=&quot;3455&quot; data-end=&quot;3509&quot;&gt;6+ years of professional experience in Game Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1k3ylkv&quot; data-start=&quot;3510&quot; data-end=&quot;3628&quot;&gt;Expertise in at least one of the following: Combat Mechanics, Combat Feel, Combat AI, or Character/Camera/Controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;zodoya&quot; data-start=&quot;3629&quot; data-end=&quot;3732&quot;&gt;3+ years of experience with Unreal Engine (including tools such as Blueprint or equivalent systems)&lt;/li&gt;
