&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For this role, you&#39;ll find success through craft expertise, a collaborative spirit, and decision-making that prioritizes the delight of players. We will be looking at your past studies, experience, and your personal relationship with games.

&lt;p&gt;Riot Games was established in 2006 by entrepreneurial gamers who believe that player-focused game development can result in great games. In 2009, Riot released its debut title&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;to critical and player acclaim. As the most played video game in the world, over 100 million play every month. Players form the foundation of our community and it’s for them that we continue to evolve and improve the&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for humble but ambitious, razor-sharp professionals who can teach us a thing or two. We promise to return the favor. Like us, you take play seriously; you’re passionate about games. We embrace those who see things differently, aren’t afraid to experiment, and who have a healthy disregard for constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&#39;s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;在 Riot，技术美术负责搭建和优化美术内容生产的技术基础、工作流程与工具体系，帮助团队以高质量、可持续的方式进行内容创作。他们需要将艺术目标转化为可执行的技术方案，持续优化流程与制作标准，并与多个职能紧密合作，消除制作中的技术阻碍，同时守住内容质量。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;作为未公开项目的资深技术美术 - 动画方向，你将专注于动画相关的技术方案设计与引擎落地，帮助团队建立稳定、可扩展的动画技术基础。你将与动画、美术指导、设计、工程以及其他技术美术成员紧密合作，将艺术表现目标转化为可执行的技术实现，并持续提升动画内容在引擎中的质量、稳定性与制作效率。你将汇报给技术美术负责人，并在推进动画技术能力建设的同时，兼顾角色绑定系统的长期发展。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;工作职责&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;负责高优先级引擎动画效果的技术方案设计与落地，包括动画状态机、IK、角色物理及相关动画技术能力建设&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;跨团队紧密协作，将动作表现、镜头需求及视觉目标转化为可执行的技术方案，并持续提升动画内容的整体表现质量与制作标准。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;识别并解决实时动画及动画资产制作过程中的关键技术问题，推进引擎内实现、联调与优化，持续改进动画资产规格，提升落地效率与实现稳定性&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;搭建、维护并优化角色、生物、道具以及表演相关需求的绑定与动画技术方案&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;开发和推动面向动画制作与效率工具、调试流程方案，帮助团队更高质量、更高效率地完成内容实现&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;能力要求&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 年及以上游戏或相关行业技术美术经验，并在技术动画方向有扎实的实操经验&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;具备从效果目标出发，进行技术抽象与方案判断的能力，能够在动画表现、玩法需求、实现成本与长期可维护性之间做出合理权衡&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;具备扎实的 Unreal Engine 经验，熟悉蓝图、动画状态机、IK 工作流、角色物理、镜头相关等实现&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;熟悉 Maya 绑定工作流程与相关功能使用，理解角色绑定与动画系统的基础实现逻辑&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;优秀的跨职能沟通与协作能力&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;优先条件&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;熟悉英雄联盟IP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;有主导角色绑定系统开发的经验，或具备基于 Maya 的 Python 脚本开发能力&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;熟悉风格化角色或变形角色的绑定方案与实现方式&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;有影视叙事、表演类高规格角色制作流程的相关经验&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For this role, you&#39;ll find success through craft expertise, a collaborative spirit, and decision-making that prioritizes the delight of players. We will be looking at your past studies, experience, and your personal relationship with games. If you embody player empathy and care about players&#39; experiences, this could be your role!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;作为申请过程的一部分，我们希望候选人提供作品集或演示demo，并且可能被要求完成艺术测试。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, Web/Full Stack to join our &lt;strong&gt;Scopely Explore Player Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;team in Mexico City on a hybrid basis, working 3 days a week from the hub.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an execution-focused Software Engineer, Web/Full Stack. We look for engineers with a strong technical background, great execution, and a self-starter mentality. In this role, you will be a key individual contributor focused on developing and scaling the critical web applications and player-facing features that support the global Pokémon GO community. You will build highly interactive, responsive web experiences while ensuring seamless data integration with our backend services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building well-designed, highly performant, and reusable web applications and UI components using React, Next.js, and TypeScript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Crafting delightful, low-latency user interfaces that deliver a seamless experience across desktop and mobile browsers for millions of active players&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implementing and maintaining backend services and APIs that reliably serve data to your web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and implementing efficient client-server contracts utilizing a modern suite of network protocols, including HTTP, GraphQL, and gRPC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating closely between engineering, design, and product teams to ensure the goals of the product are aligned with the delivered web features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participating in code reviews, writing comprehensive unit tests, and conducting troubleshooting to ensure uptime for live production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with cross-functional team members and stakeholders to cultivate strong working relationships, including regular and reliable attendance and participation in meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS, MS, or PhD in Computer Science, related technical field or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional industry experience in full-stack web development within a technology or gaming company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, production-proven experience building web applications with TypeScript, React, and framework architectures like Next.js&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of client-server application domains, with practical experience querying data and managing network communication via HTTP, GraphQL, and gRPC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to integrate modern AI coding assistants into your daily workflow to streamline development, while ensuring all AI-generated contributions meet team standards for safety, architecture, and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently, take on ambiguous challenges, and break down goals into concrete tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and adapt to changing priorities, solve ambiguous problems, and communicate proactively when plans shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on cross-functional teams with the ability to communicate effectively through written and verbal communications, including synchronous interactions with others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong English language skills are required for this role as we have a highly diverse and global business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt

&lt;p&gt;Technical Game Designers on the Teamfight Tactics team are game designers who also have access to the C++ code base. They apply the team’s engineering principles to technical design work, improve and add to existing design tools to unblock design tasks (sometimes unblocking themselves, in their game design role!), and own gameplay and systems design areas. Their game design expertise lets them dream up and create memorable gameplay experiences for TFT players, and their technical expertise lets them deliver those experiences in a robust, sustainable, and elegant way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Technical Design Manager on the Teamfight Tactics team&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll manage Technical Game Designers across the project. You&#39;ll see to their career progress, evaluate their technical and game design contributions, bring out their best work, and ensure they&#39;re delivering on their teams&#39; goals. In turn, you&#39;ll report to the Design Director, helping to build the Technical Game Design subdiscipline on the team and for League Studios, and maximizing the TD group’s impact. But: on the Teamfight Tactics team, design managers often take on individual contributions, so you’ll have plenty of chances to exercise your own craft as well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the project’s technical game designers: help them grow, learn, and perform to their potential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high craft bar: Ensure that the work you oversee meets Riot&#39;s demanding craft standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for players: Stay in tune with the player experience and know how to understand and incorporate their feedback into roadmaps and feature decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and build trust: Work closely with other discipline leads and managers to ensure Tech Design is delivering what they need, when they need it; ensure that features can be scoped efficiently so project plans can be built; and foster relationships with teams outside of Teamfight Tactics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong teams: Take an active role in recruiting and onboarding to ensure capable technical game designers join our teams and ramp up quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience as a technical game designer, gameplay engineer, or some similar position closely associated with both technical and game design work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience as a manager, team lead, or discipline leader (can overlap with the above requirement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft: Craft interviews for this role will look at both gameplay engineering and game design skills; we’d like to see Senior level craft expertise in one, but not necessarily both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Management: You&#39;ll need leadership experience resolving conflict within and across teams and fostering healthy team culture, along with examples of managing other designers with positive results: promotion, performance improvement, and strong delivery to players&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High familiarity with Teamfight Tactics, or willingness to rapidly build that familiarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience as a manager or team lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience as a technical game designer or gameplay engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing both junior and senior designers or engineers - striking the right balance of assistance and autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a live service game&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep engagement with Teamfight Tactics over multiple sets&lt;/li&gt;
